{"id":587,"date":"2020-10-29T13:31:19","date_gmt":"2020-10-29T20:31:19","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=587"},"modified":"2024-08-30T10:03:40","modified_gmt":"2024-08-30T17:03:40","slug":"led","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/led\/","title":{"rendered":"1F: LED"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef94752\" name=\"6a2213ef94752\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Getting Started<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to pair to Blockly <a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/cdmb-pairing\/\">here<\/a>.[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef948a9\" name=\"6a2213ef948a9\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your CoDrone Mini has 1 RGB LED on the main body. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. A solid LED means your drone is connected, while a flashing LED means it\u2019s in pairing mode or the battery is low.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef94944\" name=\"6a2213ef94944\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Solid LED<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To use any of the LED blocks, go to the purple lights menu.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;588&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For a solid LED, meaning it consistently stays the same color without any flashing, use the &#8220;set color to _ with a brightness of _&#8221; block.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;589&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This block has two parameters, or characteristics:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Color &#8211;<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">To change the color of the LEDs, click on the color. It will bring up a menu so that you can choose which color you want to change your CoDrone LED to.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;592&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<b>Brightness &#8211;<\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> How bright the LED is, with 0 being off and 100 being maximum brightness. The brightness value will never be negative!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef949ab\" name=\"6a2213ef949ab\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Other LED blocks<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The turn off block does exactly what it says &#8212; it turns either the LED off. The reset LED block is a little like a factory reset, but only for the LED. After using this, your LED will go back to solid red.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;597&#8243; img_size=&#8221;medium&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef949fe\" name=\"6a2213ef949fe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED rainbow<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pair to CoDrone Mini and practice using the LED to make a rainbow. Make sure each color shows for one second before switching to the next color. For optimal brightness, set it to 100. Use the wait block for one second in between the color blocks so you can see each color before it moves on to the next one. Have the pattern repeat using a loop!<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;599&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef94a4b\" name=\"6a2213ef94a4b\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 6<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Adding flight commands<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">If you want to see LEDs in flight, just drag and drop the LED block into your flight program, or drag and drop the flight command block into your LED program! Try this code to see what happens.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;601&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2213ef94aba\" name=\"6a2213ef94aba\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 7<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Spy Mission<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first system of electrical telecommunication was the telegraph. It was a device that sent pulses of electricity, either long or short, to send messages. Letters were defined by unique combinations of long and short beeps, called Morse Code. Do you recognize this message?<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>. . . _ _ _ . . .<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This message reads SOS! Look up the <\/span><a href=\"http:\/\/www.codebug.org.uk\/learn\/step\/540\/morse-code-alphabet\/\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Morse Code alphabet<\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> and learn some letters. Try coming up with a method to send messages using Morse Code with your CoDrone Mini. If you want, pair up to decode each other\u2019s messages. Send long and short flashes to send your messages using different values for the wait block.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 8 Getting Started [vc_column_text]Make sure that your CoDrone Mini is paired before starting the lesson! If you forgot how to do this, make sure to review how to&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/led\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1687,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":true,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":407,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2125,2124,2120,2122],"class_list":["post-587","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone-mini","lesson-tag-junior","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","module-junior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/587","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":12,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/587\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":9102,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/587\/revisions\/9102"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1687"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=587"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=587"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=587"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}